ata/1832332/000119312526222736/0001193125-26-222736-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-222736"}],"bear":[{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 32.8% to 31.7% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1832332/000119312526222736/0001193125-26-222736-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-222736"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 7.7% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1832332/000119312526222736/0001193125-26-222736-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-222736"},{"text":"Debt of $1.3bn against equity of $240.1m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1832332/000119312526222736/0001193125-26-222736-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-222736"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 69.6% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (31,852,763 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1832332/000119312526293937/0001193125-26-293937-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 24.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.24,"consecutive":2,"current":0.317,"current_display":"31.7%","threshold_display":"24.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather tha